# Notices

quake2midi is MIT licensed ([`LICENSE`](LICENSE)). It uses the following
third-party sources and libraries.

## Data

- **Earthquake events** — EMSC / SeismicPortal FDSN event service,
  <https://www.seismicportal.eu/fdsnws/event/1/query>. Events are fetched at
  runtime and are not stored or redistributed by this project. The fetch asks
  for a one-hour window, because the service publishes an event up to about
  21 minutes after it happens and its `start` filter applies to origin time.
  SeismicPortal data is provided by the European-Mediterranean Seismological
  Centre; consult their terms at <https://www.seismicportal.eu/>.

## Software

- **mido** — MIDI I/O for Python, MIT licence,
  <https://github.com/mido/mido>.
- **python-rtmidi** — the RtMidi binding behind mido's port access, MIT
  licence, <https://github.com/SpotlightKid/python-rtmidi>. RtMidi itself is
  under a modified MIT licence.

## MIDI ports

This project sends to a local MIDI port only. Creating one is the user's
responsibility: the IAC Driver on macOS (Apple, part of macOS), `snd-virmidi`
on Linux (the kernel's ALSA virtual MIDI driver), or a third-party loopback
such as loopMIDI on Windows (Tobias Erichsen, not bundled).